<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_VentKiln.xml                       UtinniPatches · FORGE_MECHANICS_1 F6
  ============================================================================
  forge_kit_spec.md F6 "geothermal industry — XML only": "RUT_VentSmelter /
  RUT_VentKiln / RUT_VentForge... Recipes mirror the fueled vanilla
  equivalents."

  🔴 HONEST SUBSTITUTION, checked and documented, not guessed: there is NO
  "Kiln" ThingDef anywhere in this repo, the vanilla Core/DLC Data folders,
  or the live ~599-mod installed set. Checked three ways this pass: (1)
  RimSage's own def index (`search_defs query="Kiln" defType="ThingDef"` ->
  zero results), (2) a full-text grep of every Data/*/Defs tree
  (Core/Biotech/Ideology/Odyssey/Anomaly/Royalty) for "kiln" case-
  insensitive -> zero hits, (3) a defName grep across the Steam Workshop
  content root -> zero hits (timed out at full breadth but RimSage's own
  index, which covers the live ~599-mod set this repo actually runs, is
  authoritative and already answered zero). So "the vanilla ...kiln...
  workbench def" this task asked to find does not exist to crib from.

  Judgment call, stated plainly: cribbed vanilla TableStonecutter instead
  (Core/Defs/ThingDefs_Buildings/Buildings_Production.xml) — the closest
  vanilla production building to "a kiln" in the family's absence: a
  heat/mineral-processing bench (thingClass Building_WorkTable_HeatPush,
  same as ElectricSmelter) that needs no fuel AND no power in vanilla
  already (unlike the smithy pair), so "free heat, free power" costs it
  nothing to strip — a closer fit than forcing a second smithy-shaped def to
  stand in for "kiln." Recipes mirror it the same way RUT_VentForge mirrors
  FueledSmithy: TableStonecutter's own recipeUsers entry lives on the
  RecipeDef side (Core/Defs/RecipeDefs/Recipes_Production.xml, the abstract
  `MakeStoneBlocksBase` RecipeDef, confirmed the ONE such node in the
  indexed set) rather than on the ThingDef itself, so
  RUT_VentKiln_RecipeWiring.xml (this same pass) patches that RecipeDef's
  own recipeUsers list rather than copying a static list.

  No CompProperties_AffectedByFacilities (TableStonecutter's own
  ToolCabinet linkage — a facility-bonus system unrelated to fuel/power,
  left off only to keep this def minimal; nothing bans re-adding it later).
  thingClass plain Building_WorkTable (dropping TableStonecutter's own
  _HeatPush variant for the same reason RUT_VentSmelter.xml drops it: no
  power comp to gate a heat push on).

  Placement/size/placeWorkers/WorkTableWorkSpeedFactor: same shape as
  RUT_VentSmelter.xml/RUT_VentForge.xml — see those files.

  researchPrerequisites keeps Stonecutting (TableStonecutter's own prereq:
  knowing how to cut stone is independent of what powers the bench).

  Costs/stats: INVENTED. TableStonecutter itself is stuff-costed
  (costStuffCount + stuffCategories, paintable) — simplified here to a flat
  costList, matching every other Vent* def in this pass and RUT_ScaldVent/
  RUT_SteamCatch's own precedent of dropping stuff-coloring for a fixed
  vent-locked building.

  🔴 Texture: intended to reuse vanilla TableStonecutter's own art
  (Things/Building/Production/TableStonecutter) as a placeholder, but
  validate_patch.py flags that choice as a hard ERROR under its own-
  namespace heuristic — see RUT_VentSmelter.xml's own header for the full
  reasoning. Points at its own new texPath instead
  (Things/Building/Production/RUT_VentKiln) and is held via
  src/DEPLOY_HOLD.txt until art lands.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="BenchBase">
    <defName>RUT_VentKiln</defName>
    <label>vent kiln</label>
    <description>A stonecutter's kiln built directly over a steam vent — no fuel, no power line, the vent alone runs it hot enough. The one place fire costs nothing.</description>
    <thingClass>Building_WorkTable</thingClass>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Production/RUT_VentKiln</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(2,2)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <altitudeLayer>Building</altitudeLayer>
    <fillPercent>0.5</fillPercent>
    <useHitPoints>True</useHitPoints>
    <statBases>
      <WorkToBuild>2000</WorkToBuild>
      <MaxHitPoints>180</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>1.0</Flammability>
      <Cleanliness>-5</Cleanliness>
      <WorkTableWorkSpeedFactor>1.2</WorkTableWorkSpeedFactor>
    </statBases>
    <size>(2,2)</size>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <scatterableOnMapGen>false</scatterableOnMapGen>
    <designationCategory>Production</designationCategory>
    <passability>PassThroughOnly</passability>
    <pathCost>50</pathCost>
    <hasInteractionCell>True</hasInteractionCell>
    <interactionCellOffset>(0,0,-1)</interactionCellOffset>
    <surfaceType>Item</surfaceType>
    <costList>
      <Steel>30</Steel>
    </costList>
    <inspectorTabs>
      <li>ITab_Bills</li>
    </inspectorTabs>
    <placeWorkers>
      <li>PlaceWorker_OnSteamGeyser</li>
    </placeWorkers>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>Stonecutting</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
